/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  Benchmark C -- the thermophysical system, Choupo's own.

  Two liquid phases on ONE NRTL surface: the ternary set of Choi & Rhim,
  Hwahak Konghak 24(3) (1986) 185-194, Table 3 -- fitted by the authors to
  their own measured water + acetone + MIBK tie lines at 25 C -- carried as
  three case-local pair records in constant/parameters/NRTL/ (each says
  where its numbers come from and how they were converted).  The NRTL reads
  them from there by the pair's name.  The transcription is checked by
  benchmarks/dwsim/compare.py against the authors' own calculated tie
  lines (measurements/choiRhim1986_table6_mibk_nrtl.csv).

  WHY NOT UNIFAC ALONE (measured 2026-10-20, README): Choupo's UNIFAC (the
  VLE parameterisation, UNIFAC.H) does predict a water/MIBK gap at 25 C,
  but puts its water-rich branch at the LL flash's 1e-4 simplex floor and
  its organic branch at 20 mol % water, where Choi & Rhim measured 0.38 mol %
  MIBK and 11.8 mol % water (their Table 5).  Vitor approved curating an LLE
  set from primary measurements in that case (DEV.md 4c C123).  The UNIFAC
  system is kept as variants/unifac/constant/thermoPhysPropDict and run by
  the comparison script beside this one.

  The reference sample uses neither: its package is a modified (Dortmund)
  UNIFAC; no parameter of theirs is used here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

recordType    thermophysicalPropertySystem;
schemaVersion 2;

components ( water acetone methylIsobutylKetone );

equilibrium
{
    formulation gammaGamma;

    liquid { activityModel { model NRTL; } }   // pairs: constant/parameters/NRTL/

    liquidPhases
    (
        { name raffinate; }
        { name extract; }
    );
}
